            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 8,
              "start": 8
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito asked if any threat of serious injury is sufficient."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "6eecd173282b39919a4a0086e23c8d35fbfdb621b68918c14d432c858adfad11",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6eecd173282b-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, justice Scalia questioned the relevance of an \u201cunprovable question.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "6eecd173282b39919a4a0086e23c8d35fbfdb621b68918c14d432c858adfad11",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6eecd173282b-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer asked why the petitioner answered \u201cyes\u201d to Justice Alito\u2019s question and whether the Attorney General would retain broad discretion over the duress defense."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "6eecd173282b39919a4a0086e23c8d35fbfdb621b68918c14d432c858adfad11",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6eecd173282b-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Stevens referenced the Fedorenko case and asked whether the Court is assuming the petitioner\u2019s truthfulness."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "6eecd173282b39919a4a0086e23c8d35fbfdb621b68918c14d432c858adfad11",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6eecd173282b-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked whether the coercion defense is solely within the Attorney General\u2019s discretion."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "6eecd173282b39919a4a0086e23c8d35fbfdb621b68918c14d432c858adfad11",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6eecd173282b-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 25,
              "start": 25
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked what the minimum culpability standard the Attorney General could impose would be."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "6eecd173282b39919a4a0086e23c8d35fbfdb621b68918c14d432c858adfad11",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6eecd173282b-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 25,
              "start": 25
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Souter asked whether serious bodily harm satisfies the duress requirement."
      }
